.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH RANMA-LOGS 1 "" "ranma 0.4.0" "ranma manual"
.SH NAME
ranma\-logs \- Print the end of ranma\*(Aqs log (\fB~/.local/state/ranma/ranma.log\fR): errors in full, and what the servers did. Read off the file, so it works with no server running
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBranma logs\fR [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-lines\fR] [\fB\-\-path\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the end of ranma\*(Aqs log (\fB~/.local/state/ranma/ranma.log\fR): errors in full, and what the servers did. Read off the file, so it works with no server running
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-lines\fR \fI<LINES>\fR [default: 50]
How many entries (an error with its traceback is one)
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR
Print the log\*(Aqs path instead
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBranma\fR(1)
